{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Planarity on undirected graphs. Self-loops and parallel edges never change an answer: the tests"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"run on the underlying simple graph, read once through the rows in index space. A directed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph’s planarity is that of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"graph.undirectedView"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","text":"Graph","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"isPlanar","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"planarEmbedding()"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isOuterplanar"},{"type":"text","text":" run the left-right planarity test (de"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Fraysseix and Rosenstiehl, in Brandes’s formulation, 2009); "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"findKuratowskiSubgraph()"},{"type":"text","text":" runs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Boyer and Myrvold’s edge-addition algorithm (2004), whose failure state isolates the witness."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"All are O(n + m), iterative, and deterministic: graphs with the same rows (the same vertices in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same order, the same edge positions, the same incidence order) get the same embedding and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same witness."}]}]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity","doc:\/\/Planarity\/document